            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I think there are some subtle cases, which maybe aren't important to handle, of r-value references and const/volatile combinations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you see this as a non-starter, or should I get it cleaned up so we can merge it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Did you test this being built against openbmc/openbmc?  If this were the write path, I wouldn't expect it to work, since there would be a lot of `const foo`s that don't match the `is_same` checks, but since this is the read path maybe it works fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> Did you test this being built against openbmc/openbmc?\n\nYes, openbmc master builds just fine.  I built S7106, but I'd assume all the other targets would build as well.  I ran through a couple redfish commands (just because that's what I have set up, not because it's the best possible test) just to make sure the basic read/append things work, and it seems to work just fine.\n\n>  If this were the write path, I wouldn't expect it to work, since there would be a lot of `const foo`s that don't match the `is_same` checks, but since this is the read path maybe it works fine.\n\nAgreed.  In the write path, I would expect we'd need to do a std::decay_v on the main template param to get rid of the const/volatileness to deduplicate the parameters, but I haven't looked at that much yet.  For whatever reason, the Append path doesn't show up in compile-time profiles as much, but I intend to do that at some point."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
